{
  "summary": "P1 credential phishing, Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5, aisha.khan@brightline.example, device BL-LT-0105). Reported: she clicked the link in a \"payroll verification\" email and typed her password into the page. Click time not given in the ticket. The matching lure is probably Q-1003, \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\" from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I for l), received 2026-10-09 08:55 UTC and quarantined as phishing (not releasable). A copy likely reached her inbox, or she got it some other way. Checked: account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, password last set 2026-09-09. Duo push enrolled on her phone. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days: 9 sign-ins, all successful from New York (corporate 203.0.113.10 / residential 198.51.100.25) at 09:35 local, no hosting networks, no MFA denials. The latest is 2026-10-08, so nothing after the phishing email arrived. Nothing suspicious, so I did NOT request block_sign_in. Requested: password reset (pending tech approval), temp password to be given by phone after callback verification. Still needed: confirm the click time and whether she approved any Duo push; revoke active sessions/tokens; check mailbox rules/forwarding; check whether other users got the same lure (an HR/payroll-themed lookalike domain) and purge it; keep watching sign-ins.",
  "reason": "KB-029 says always escalate. Ticket is P1."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for telling us so quickly. That makes a big difference. Here's where things stand: we've checked your account and see no sign-ins from anyone else so far. We still have to treat the password you typed as stolen, so we've asked for a password reset. Once a technician approves it, they'll call you to confirm it's you, then give you a temporary password over the phone. You'll pick a new one the next time you sign in. Our security team is also looking into this now. Until then: 1) Please don't delete the email, because security may need it. Don't click it again or forward it to anyone. 2) If you used that same password on any other site, change it there too. 3) Don't approve any Duo push on your phone that you didn't start yourself. If you get one you didn't expect, tap Deny and let us know right away. 4) If you remember about what time you clicked the link, or if you approved a Duo prompt afterward, please reply and tell us. Thanks again for reporting this so fast.",
  "internal_note": "P1 phishing credential entry, followed KB-029/KB-008. User: Aisha Khan (user_id 5), HR, account active, not blocked, Duo push enrolled. Matching lure: quarantined message Q-1003 'Urgent: verify your payroll login' from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain), received 2026-10-09 08:55 UTC, marked phishing and not releasable. Do not release. Sign-in logs (14 days): 9 successes, all from New York on her usual corporate/residential IPs, no hosting networks, no MFA denials, latest 2026-10-08. Nothing after the lure arrived. No suspicious activity, so block_sign_in was not requested. reset_password queued (approval id 1). Deliver the temp password only by phone after callback verification. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) for session revocation, mailbox rule/forwarding review, a check for other recipients of the lure, and continued monitoring. Click time still unknown; I asked the user for it.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-029",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
